==Swedish==

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|Sv-en kontinent.ogg|audio}}

===Noun===
{{infl|sv|noun|c}}
{{sv-noun-reg-er}}

# {{context|geology|lang=sv}} [[continent]]; a large contiguous landmass

====Compounds====
* [[superkontinent]]

====Usage notes====
Depending on how one makes the divisions, one may count between 4 and 7 ''kontinenter'' on Earth, maybe most often 5 or 6 (Antarctic, Eurasia, Africa, Australia, and finally the Americas as either one or two). Only rarely would Europe and Asia be considered separate ''kontinenter''.
In contrast, the word ''[[världsdel]]'' denotes a cultural or historical division, comparable in size to a ''kontinent''. This division  is always done into 7 parts: [[Antarktis]], [[Sydamerika]], [[Nordamerika]], [[Europa]], [[Asien]], [[Afrika]] and [[Oceanien]].

